CLI build needs DevEco's bundled JBR, otherwise PackageHap fails with 00308018 "Unable to locate a Java Runtime":
JAVA_HOME=/Applications/DevEco-Studio.app/Contents/jbr/Contents/Home, DEVECO_SDK_HOME=/Applications/DevEco-Studio.app/Contents/sdk, node from Contents/tools/node/bin, run `node Contents/tools/hvigor/bin/hvigorw.js ... assembleHap --no-daemon`. Output is unsigned HAP; `hdc install -r` works on emulator 127.0.0.1:5555 (bundle com.hefengbao.jingmo.hw).

As of 2026-10-14 the emulator initially had content data only for 成语. After user enabled emulator network (same day), synced via 设置→同步数据: 经典诗文, 歌词, 诗歌, 谚语, 谜语, 歇后语. NOT synced: 诗文 (1.6M rows, heavy), 人物 (DNS failed again — emulator network is flaky). Test bookmarks left on device: 时间情缘/幻象/分房制度被取消/织布机上的梭子/四月八…/长恨歌 + 4 idioms. Baseline tag: baseline-jm-spec7 → 264a375.

**Why:** competition rules forbid fetching upstream; the app is offline-data, so only idiom flows can be run locally.
**How to apply:** for lyric/poetry/riddle/wisecrack/classicpoem flows, ask user for an import data file or network before claiming runtime verification.
